   "notes": "Described the decoder block; the encoder block is the same without cross-attention and with non-causal self-attention. Base (6+6 layers, d=768) is the smallest configuration; large (12+12, d=1024) is the main pre-trained model. The paper declares the Vaswani et al. Transformer as its ancestor, so post-LayerNorm, residual connections and dense exact attention are marked inherited. Positional embeddings are marked learned because the paper says they are updated during MT fine-tuning, which differs from the ancestor's sinusoidal encoding. These are not stated: heads, d_ff, vocab size (only 'same BPE as GPT-2'), context length, eps, biases, embedding tying, and the GeLU form (exact or tanh). The machine-translation source encoder and the classification heads are fine-tuning additions and are not included."
